# Setup a Repo

Configure one named repo to COE-ELSD-081..087 and its `AGENTS.md`
(`../../docs/coe/engineering-lifecycle-secure-delivery/engineering-lifecycle-secure-delivery.sdoc`).
`alphazede/azedge` `.github/` is the worked reference: adopt by applicability, never blind copy.

## Preconditions

Require `owner/repo`, path, baseline ref, approved profile (`public-pr`,
`private-collaborative-pr`, `private-owner-direct`), and repo-scoped authority (COE-ELSD-085).
Honor prior authority; missing authority stops mutation but allows read-only audit.

## Configure

1. **Inspect** — `gh api repos/O/R` for `security_and_analysis`, `properties/values`,
   `rulesets`, `code-scanning/default-setup`; list maintained manifest roots and languages.
2. **Profile** — set custom property `delivery_profile` to the approved value.
3. **Floor** — classify every returned `security_and_analysis` key by applicability, then PATCH
   `repos/O/R` with a `security_and_analysis` body enabling approved controls:
   `dependabot_security_updates`, `secret_scanning`,
   `secret_scanning_push_protection`, `secret_scanning_ai_detection`,
   `secret_scanning_non_provider_patterns`, `secret_scanning_validity_checks`. Classify
   `secret_scanning_delegated_alert_dismissal` and `secret_scanning_delegated_bypass` separately
   as active authority workflows — no blind enablement, no invented waiver. Keep `deletion` and
   `non_fast_forward` on the default branch.
4. **Dependabot** — `.github/dependabot.yml`: routine *version* updates grouped per
   maintained ecosystem root at `interval: monthly`. Security updates stay enabled
   independently of that cadence.
5. **CodeQL** — paid private Code Security scope: `azedge`, `requirements-system`,
   `Alphazedehq`; expansion requires owner direction. Private recipe: only
   `workflow_dispatch`, SHA-pinned actions, one matrix entry per applicable language,
   `build-mode: none` unless a build is required. Preserve public PR analysis and the existing
   language and query coverage. Cut over: land the verified workflow, disable the conflicting
   default setup, read manual availability back; stop on failure without restoring automation.
6. **Gates** — for `private-owner-direct`, local gates own routine checks; hosted
   Quality/CI uses only `workflow_dispatch`. Update trigger-contract checks together.
   Preserve public/collaborative PR gates and remote release/signing evidence.
   Keep organization Actions and AI-credit paid-overage budgets at zero with hard stops;
   keep Code Quality disabled. Budget exhaustion blocks required hosted evidence.

## Verify

Read back each changed setting and file exactly. Configuration is not operational proof: never re-run
broad validation or a full scan on an equivalent configuration; add focused checks only
for a material difference or actual failure. Integrate by `$ship-pull-request` under PR
profiles, gated fast-forward under `private-owner-direct`, withholding on any failing or
unavailable gate (COE-ELSD-086). At most three evidence-driven rounds; roll back only your
changes. Return `PASS`, `CONTRACT_FAILURE`, `NEEDS_MORE_EVIDENCE`, `REPAIRABLE_FAILURE`,
`ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE` or `OWNER_DECISION_REQUIRED` with paths, commands, readbacks, blocker.
