# Test Engineering
Select one V&V method and produce objective evidence with a pass/fail rule.
Executable product tests exist only when the method is test.

## Preconditions

Require the requirement or named behavior, intended use, observable change,
and write authority. Cite S8 [SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH](../engineering-methods/references/standards-receipts.md) for Appendix I structure.

## Procedure

1. Plan the V&V bound: requirement, intended use, and whether observable
   behavior changed. `NO_TEST_REQUIRED` is valid only when none changed.
2. Design: select exactly one of analysis, inspection, demonstration, test,
   or evaluation. Record required evidence and pass/fail. If lineup/model
   choice or RS publication is requested, return a typed gap.
3. Implement only where applicable. If method is test, hand executable-test
   work to write-tests. Non-test methods emit inspection, analysis,
   demonstration, or evaluation evidence, never product test code.
4. Execute the selected method. Collect the recorded evidence.
5. Evaluate pass/fail. Ponytail active, inactive, or unavailable must leave
   required cases, assertions, evidence, traceability, and coverage identical.
6. Interface obligations: define positive and negative cases for every
   `APPLICABLE` field in [interface-completeness-profile](../requirements-engineering/references/interface-completeness-profile.md).
   One-sided cases fail that profile check.

## Authority

TE owns V&V method and evidence design. RE owns requirement quality; SysML
Modeling owns semantic method; Integration Engineering owns progressive
assembly; RS owns SDoc/SysML content, relationships, revision, validation,
review, and publication; Bearing Lite owns execution planning, lineup, SEIT
orchestration, graph, slices, and dispatch. Do not invent hook paths or TE
receipt schema. Do not duplicate a normative store.

## Bounds

At most three evidence-driven corrections. Apply [quality-gate](references/quality-gate.md),
[vnv-plan](references/vnv-plan.md), and [verification-case](references/verification-case.md).

## Outcomes

Return exactly one: `PASS` with method, evidence, and pass/fail; `FAIL`;
`NO_TEST_REQUIRED`; `TYPED_GAP`; `UNAVAILABLE`; `NEEDS_EVIDENCE`; or `BLOCKED`.

Never turn a non-test method into product tests, let Ponytail reduce coverage, or use `NO_TEST_REQUIRED` to evade a changed behavior's V&V.
